{"id":"9b3d28329836fc3d86c33da8723289df66d9f362","axis":"silent","repo":"numpy/numpy","sha":"9b3d28329836fc3d86c33da8723289df66d9f362","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"doc/source/reference/c-api/array.rst","lines":["@@ -1829,7 +1829,22 @@ the functions that must be implemented for each slot.","    Sets the loop to use for an operation at runtime. The *context* is the","    runtime context for the operation. *aligned* indicates whether the data","    access for the loop is aligned (1) or unaligned (0). *move_references*","-   indicates whether embedded references in the data should be copied. *strides*","+   is only set for casts. A cast normally leaves its input untouched. If","+   *move_references* is nonzero, the cast is a move instead of a copy: NumPy","+   does not clean up the input after a successful cast, so once the loop has","+   converted an input element it must release whatever the element owns, for","+   example by decrementing the reference count of an object or freeing a","+   heap-allocated buffer, or transfer it to the output. The loop must leave","+   each converted element safe to clear again, for example by zeroing it,","+   because NumPy reuses its temporary buffers and clears the whole input if","+   the loop fails. NumPy sets it when the input is one of its own","+   temporary buffers, such as the buffer a ufunc computes its results into","+   when the output array has a different dtype, or the intermediate buffer","+   of a cast that takes more than one step. When ``NPY_METH_get_loop`` is","+   not defined, NumPy handles this itself: it runs the","+   ``NPY_METH_strided_loop`` or ``NPY_METH_unaligned_strided_loop`` and then","+   clears the input elements with the ``NPY_DT_get_clear_loop`` of the input","+   DType. *strides*","    are the strides for the input array, *out_loop* is a pointer that must be","    filled in with a pointer to the loop implementation. *out_transferdata* can","    be optionally filled in to allow passing in extra user-defined context to an"],"additions":16,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"numpy/_core/src/multiarray/array_method.c","lines":["@@ -40,6 +40,7 @@"," #include \"common.h\""," #include \"numpy/ufuncobject.h\""," #include \"dtype_transfer.h\"","+#include \"dtype_traversal.h\""," "," "," /*","@@ -116,6 +117,88 @@ is_contiguous("," }"," "," ","+typedef struct {","+    NpyAuxData base;","+    PyArrayMethod_StridedLoop *loop;","+    NPY_traverse_info clear;","+} move_references_auxdata;","+","+","+static void","+move_references_auxdata_free(NpyAuxData *auxdata)","+{","+    move_references_auxdata *data = (move_references_auxdata *)auxdata;","+    NPY_traverse_info_xfree(&data->clear);","+    PyMem_Free(data);","+}","+","+","+static NpyAuxData *","+move_references_auxdata_clone(NpyAuxData *auxdata)","+{","+    move_references_auxdata *data = (move_references_auxdata *)auxdata;","+    move_references_auxdata *res = PyMem_Malloc(sizeof(move_references_auxdata));","+    if (res == NULL) {","+        return NULL;","+    }","+    res->base = data->base;","+    res->loop = data->loop;","+    if (NPY_traverse_info_copy(&res->clear, &data->clear) < 0) {","+        PyMem_Free(res);","+        return NULL;","+    }","+    return (NpyAuxData *)res;","+}","+","+","+/*","+ * Runs a cast loop that does not know about `move_references` and then","+ * clears the input, also when the loop failed.","+ */","+static int","+move_references_strided_loop(","+        PyArrayMethod_Context *context, char *const *data,","+        const npy_intp *dimensions, const npy_intp *strides,","+        NpyAuxData *auxdata)","+{","+    move_references_auxdata *aux = (move_references_auxdata *)auxdata;","+    int res = aux->loop(context, data, dimensions, strides, NULL);","+    if (aux->clear.func(NULL, aux->clear.descr, data[0], dimensions[0],","+                        strides[0], aux->clear.auxdata) < 0) {","+        return -1;","+    }","+    return res;","+}","+","+","+static int","+wrap_loop_to_move_references(","+        PyArrayMethod_Context *context, int aligned, const npy_intp *strides,","+        PyArrayMethod_StridedLoop **out_loop, NpyAuxData **out_transferdata,","+        NPY_ARRAYMETHOD_FLAGS *flags)","+{","+    move_references_auxdata *data = PyMem_Malloc(sizeof(move_references_auxdata));","+    if (data == NULL) {","+        PyErr_NoMemory();","+        return -1;","+    }","+    NPY_ARRAYMETHOD_FLAGS clear_flags;","+    if (PyArray_GetClearFunction(","+            aligned, strides[0], context->descriptors[0],","+            &data->clear, &clear_flags) < 0) {","+        PyMem_Free(data);","+        return -1;","+    }","+    data->base.free = &move_references_auxdata_free;","+    data->base.clone = &move_references_auxdata_clone;","+    data->loop = *out_loop;","+    *out_loop = &move_references_strided_loop;","+    *out_transferdata = (NpyAuxData *)data;","+    *flags = PyArrayMethod_COMBINED_FLAGS(*flags, clear_flags);","+    return 0;","+}","+","+"," /**","  * The default method to fetch the correct loop for a cast or ufunc","  * (at the time of writing only casts).","@@ -126,7 +209,8 @@ is_contiguous(","  *","  * @param context The arraymethod context","  * @param aligned Flag indicating data is aligned (1) or not (0)","- * param move_references UNUSED -- listed below but doxygen doesn't see as a parameter","+ * @param move_references If set, the references held by the input are","+ *        released after the loop has run.","  * @param strides Array of step sizes for each dimension of the arrays involved","  * @param out_loop Output pointer to the function that will perform the strided loop.","  * @param out_transferdata Output pointer to auxiliary data (if any)","@@ -138,7 +222,7 @@ is_contiguous("," NPY_NO_EXPORT int"," npy_default_get_strided_loop(","         PyArrayMethod_Context *context,","-        int aligned, int NPY_UNUSED(move_references), const npy_intp *strides,","+        int aligned, int move_references, const npy_intp *strides,","  